# The image build needs the Go sources and nothing else. Without this file the
# ENTIRE working tree goes to the daemon as build context — 23 MB of it, including
# the demo recordings and the lab's runtime state. That is not just slow: the lab
# writes files owned by the container user, and the build then dies with
# "checking context: no permission to read from lab/party/hub.peers" on a machine
# that has run the demos.
.git
.github
.claude

# Lab, demos and their runtime state (some of it not readable by this user).
lab
# ...with two exceptions. The lab images are built from the REPO ROOT as context
# and copy these paths out of lab/ (lab/Dockerfile:18, Dockerfile.nat:7,
# Dockerfile.firewalls:18, pentest/Dockerfile.attacker:19). Excluding lab
# wholesale made every one of those builds fail with "not found", which is how a
# lab run can quietly stop testing anything — or silently reuse a stale image.
# Named narrowly on purpose: the runtime state this exclusion exists for
# (lab/party/*.peers and friends) stays out of the context.
!lab/entrypoint-*.sh
!lab/pentest
media

# Documentation and deployment templates — none of it is copied into the image.
docs
deployments
unraid
*.md
LICENSE

# Local build output.
dist
buddynet
buddynet-handshake
